WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
Begin with a dense core inside a dark cloud.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:07.080
Gravity brings material inward. Bok globules are dusty star

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.380
formation sites; a dark appearance does not mean nothing

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.820
is happening inside. The supplied sequence develops a central

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.080
protostar, an envelope, and a rotating disk. Bipolar outflows

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.920
follow the rotation axis. Herbig Haro features are associated

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.600
with outflow activity, not a different name for the

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.700
entire dark cloud. The sequence continues through a young

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.240
star with a disk toward a stellar and planetary

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.360
system. The envelope thins and the disk changes. This

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.840
is a schematic path, not a guarantee that every

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.700
core forms one star or follows the same ages

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.088
and sizes.
